text.paragraph:
Dilute Vitamin K1 Injection with 0.9% Sodium Chloride Injection, 5% Dextrose Injection, or 5% Dextrose and Sodium Chloride Injection. Avoid use of other diluents that may contain benzyl alcohol, which can cause serious toxicity in newborns or low birth weight infants [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2), 

                              Use in Specific Populations (8.4)

                           ].

Vitamin K1 Injection contains benzyl alcohol. If available, a preservative-free phytonadione formulation is recommended when Vitamin K1 Injection is needed during lactation [see Warnings and Precautions (5.2), 

                              Use in Specific Populations (8.4)

                           ].
